# Tool Usage

Follow `docs/TOOL_USAGE_POLICY.md`.

## Must use when applicable

| Situation | Tool |
|-----------|------|
| Fresh library/API facts | WebSearch or Context7 |
| UI verification | Browser MCP / Playwright / chrome-devtools |
| File ground truth | filesystem MCP or Read |
| GitHub remote state | GitHub MCP or `gh` |
| Deterministic validation | contract-selected targeted checks; `npm run check:tooling` for the control plane; full `scripts/agent_gate.py` only in an isolated no-writeback copy |

## MCP configured but unused

If MCP was available and relevant, explain in `reports/current-cohort-report.json` → `tools_not_used`.

## Fallbacks

Record `TOOL_UNAVAILABLE` or `BLOCKED_ENV`; never invent probe results.

| Unavailable | Fallback |
|-------------|----------|
| Stitch MCP | `docs/design/stitch/` templates |
| Codex | Cursor small rounds + `docs/CODEX_HANDOFF.md` |

## Translation pipeline (summary)

Full mapping: `docs/TOOL_USAGE_POLICY.md` §11. Use local scripts + dry-run by default; quality/workbench via `run_quality_review.py` and UI rules above. Skill: `docs/agent_skills/translation_qa_skill.md`.

## Forbidden

Real API, real publish, `.env` reads, force push, browser via Multitask subagent.

Complements: `.cursor/rules/mcp-required.mdc`, `mcp-agent-tools.mdc`.
